      "writtenOn": "2025-05-20T11:55:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Indeed, thanks for catching. I think we can just remove this, this is an edge case that shouldn\u0027t matter in practice, since:\n1. the host shouldn\u0027t need to enable CR0.PG before starting pvmfw.\n2. IIUC the registers state captured in mmu-\u003ecpu_role is used by the host for things like MMIO emulation, to walk the guest\u0027s page tables to translate GVA-\u003eGPA when needed, and for pVMs the host cannot do that anyway.",
      "parentUuid": "6aac2feb_a1004ed6",
      "revId": "599fbac4bb67908de21548697a897faf9f5a0b6b",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
